+# Decision: the lab's role, where issues live, and the processes kept
+
+Justin's decisions from his interview on the afternoon of 4 October 2026, with one more from that day and three from
+3 October. Copied on 7 October 2026 from `STATE.md` (as updated 4 Oct 17:31, lines 33-34, 38-55 and 57-58), where
+they were the only record in this Scope. Copied, not re-decided; the wording is `STATE.md`'s.
+
+## 4 October, the interview
+
+- **The lab is the central Scope** for project management, core issue tracking, code quality and security. Astra is
+  to say what else it should cover.
+- **Where issues live:** a Scope's issues stay in its own repository, on one central map (orchestrator#140). A `core`
+  label marks a Scope issue that needs ORC's core changed. Later, Scopes may track their own business logic
+  elsewhere.
+- **The processes kept, all of them:**
+  - map and label check;
+  - tests on every PR (#144);
+  - the security-review and package-API checks;
+  - daily diary;
+  - weekly adversarial review;
+  - entropy guard at session end;
+  - FRICTION into rules, monthly (#60);
+  - branch and worktree cleanup (#70);
+  - `/tmp` cleanup (#182).
+- **ORC scheduling (#166) is built first,** and the scheduled processes run through it.
+- **Astra runs entropy-guard's assessment on ORC and the lab together.** Justin was shaping the brief before it ran.
+- **Labels:** the type-label proposal waits on Astra's revisions (`reports/2026-10-04-labels-review-astra.md`).
+
+## 4 October, earlier
+
+- **Moving Stillness is paused.** Browser-stack work that touches it (#118, #52, MS #52) waits.
+
+## 3 October
+
+These belong to the issues they name. They are copied here because `STATE.md` was their only record in this Scope.
+
+- #194 keeps all six preview items: a configurable limit, and fixed tailnet links.
+- Moving Stillness's `failure-verdicts` is dropped.
+- MS #52 reads every entry-list page.
